{
  "$schema": "./models.schema.json",
  "_comment": "Reconciled to live az cognitiveservices model list and subscription quota. Every deployment pins an explicit version. `reasoningEffort` lists the values the app advertises after live probes, not an exhaustive provider capability claim. Legacy values were established on 2026-07-31; GPT-6 Astra's none/low/medium/high/xhigh values were confirmed on 2026-09-06 through the governed API and proxy. Documentation and provider 'Supported values' errors are not sufficient evidence: they over-report for gpt-5.4-pro and under-report for gpt-5.4. Probe new values through SimpleL7Proxy -> APIM -> Foundry and retain the outcomes; do not introduce direct provider egress.",
  "naming": {
    "_comment": "Naming tokens for the whole stack (single source of truth). `subscriptionToken` is stamped into every model deployment name; `foundryToken` names the Foundry accounts/projects (mf-<foundryToken>-<env>-<region>). main.bicep, scripts/gen-model-catalog.py, scripts/validate-catalog.py, and app/api catalog.py all read these, so changing them here (plus AZURE_ENV_NAME) is what makes a subscription/tenant move 1:1. After changing, run scripts/gen-model-catalog.py to regenerate the runtime catalog. See docs/runbooks/greenfield-standup.md#5-select-environment-posture-and-names.",
    "subscriptionToken": "slurmfactory",
    "foundryToken": "aiforia",
    "pattern": "{model}-{subscriptionToken}-{region}-{skuShort}",
    "skuShort": {
      "GlobalStandard": "glbl",
      "DataZoneStandard": "dz",
      "Standard": "std"
    }
  },
  "regions": {
    "eastus2": {
      "dataZone": "US",
      "primary": true,
      "roles": [
        "chat",
        "voice",
        "image",
        "video"
      ]
    },
    "swedencentral": {
      "dataZone": "EU",
      "primary": true,
      "roles": [
        "chat",
        "voice",
